    "result_text": "The full suite passes. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: shared-household support on `POST /api/owners`\n\nThe `sharesHousehold` request flag and its \"skip the duplicate-household rejection\" behaviour already existed (`RequireUniqueHousehold`). What was missing was the **`householdId` assignment and response**, which I added:\n\n**New pipeline step** \u2014 `AssignHouseholdId.java`: when the request sets `sharesHousehold=true`, it computes a **stable, deterministic** household id from the normalized (trim / collapse-whitespace / lower-case) `lastName` + `address` \u2014 the same normalization `RequireUniqueHousehold` uses \u2014 as `HH-<first 12 upper-hex of SHA-256>`. Because it's derived from the household's identifying fields, every owner joining the same household gets the identical id. Owners not sharing a household are left with no `householdId`.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 inserted `assignHousehold` into `owners.POST.yml` between `build` and `assignCode`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n**Persistence & response**:\n- `Owner` entity: added `householdId` field mapped to a new `household_id` column.\n- `openapi.yml`: added `householdId` as a read-only property on the `Owner` schema (auto-generated into `OwnerDto`; MapStruct maps it by name, so it's returned on `GET /api/owners/{id}`).\n- Schema SQL: added `household_id VARCHAR(40)` to all four dialects (hsqldb/h2/postgres/mysql), and appended a trailing `NULL` to the positional seed inserts in hsqldb and mysql `data.sql` (h2/postgres use named-column inserts, so they were unaffected).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` \u2014 which creates two owners joining an existing owner's household and asserts they share a non-blank `householdId` \u2014 passes, along with the rest of the suite (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
